:''Not to be confused with [[Cats in the Stars]].''
'''Cats of the Cosmos''' (宇宙編, ''Uchū-hen'', '''Cosmos Arc'''), commonly shortened to CotC, is the third saga in [[The Battle Cats]] and is unlocked after clearing Chapter 1 of [[Into the Future]]. Like the previous sagas, it contains 3 Chapters, each with 48 stages. Cats of the Cosmos features most of the enemies introduced in Into the Future, as well as some [[:Category:Cats of the Cosmos Enemies|new enemies]] and [[:Category:Stories of Legend Enemies|Stories of Legend enemies]].

The main gimmicks of this saga are the introductions of Stage Restrictions and [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|"Starred" Alien Enemies]], which are unaffected by the [[Aqua Crystal]] and [[Plasma Crystal]] [[Treasure]]s from Into the Future. Starred Aliens have a 1,600% strength magnification by default, which can only be reduced by collecting the Treasures in Cats of the Cosmos.

Chapter 1 was added in [[Version 6.5 Update|Version 6.5]], Chapter 2 was added in [[Version 7.2 Update|Version 7.2]] and Chapter 3 was released in [[Version 8.3 Update|Version 8.3]].

[[Version 11.3 Update|Version 11.3]] brought [[Zombie Outbreaks]] to Chapter 1, [[Version 12.6 Update|Version 12.6]] brought them to Chapter 2, and [[Version 14.7 Update|Version 14.7]] brought them to Chapter 3.

==Story==
As its name suggests, Cats of the Cosmos has the [[Cat Units|Cats]] invading the cosmos and encountering more [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]], presumably using the rocket mentioned at the end of [[Into the Future]]. The ending reveals that the narrator of Cats of the Cosmos was [[The Cat God (Special Cat)|Cat God]] and that the Cats and Aliens have discussed time travel, mind control and "all kinds of obscure technical topics" with each other. It also suggests moving onward to the realm of legend, referring to [[Legend Stages]] (although Legend Stages is unlocked earlier).

In all versions except the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]], the year mentioned in the Cats of the Cosmos opening is whatever year the device's clock is set to. For example, if the current year is {{CURRENTYEAR}}, Cats of the Cosmos starts on New Year's Day of {{CURRENTYEAR}}.

