==New Features==
===Starred Aliens===
This saga introduces [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]], a subtype of [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] that can be identified by a yellow star badge on a part of their bodies. Even though they are categorized as Aliens, the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] collected in [[Into the Future]] don't affect them. Their strength magnifications are initially multiplied by 1,600%, which can only be reduced by the [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]]. Collecting all Superior Anti-Starred Alien Treasures in a Cats of the Cosmos chapter will reduce their stats by 500% each (1,600% - 1,100% - 600% - 100%).

Starred Aliens introduced in Chapter 1:
*[[Shibalien Elite]]
*[[Star Peng]]
*[[General GreGory]]
*[[Le'Solar]]
*[[Project A]]
*[[Corporal Weyland]]
*[[Spacefish Jones]]

Starred Aliens introduced in Chapter 2:
*[[UltraBaaBaa]]
*[[Kid Tappa]]
*[[Ribbo]]

Starred Aliens introduced in Chapter 3:
*[[Mesocosmocyclone]]
*[[Gardeneel Bros.]]
*[[Axoloty]]
*[[Filibuster Obstructa]]

===Treasure===
:''For the full article, see [[Treasure]].''
This saga expands the series of "elemental" [[Fruit Treasures]] that increase the effectiveness of certain abilities against a particular type of enemy. [[Titanium Fruit]] ([[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]]), [[Antimatter Fruit]] ([[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]) and [[Enigma Fruit]] ([[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]) are available to collect here as well as Treasure to increase XP earned, max [[Cat Energy]] and [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures|five sets of Treasure]] for weakening the [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]]. The last Treasure on the list is the [[Mystery Mask]], which is needed to weaken the final boss of each chapter.

===Abilities===
:''Main articles: [[Special Abilities]] and [[Barrier]]''
This saga introduces the Warp, Immune to Warp, [[Barrier]] and Barrier Breaker abilities. [[:Category:Enemies with Warp ability|Enemies with the Warp ability]] have a chance to bring one or a group of Cats they hit backward or forward a specific distance after an amount of time; [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Cats with the Immune to Warp ability]] will ignore this effect. Warped units will disappear from the battlefield until the warp duration ends, but still count toward the Cat Deploy Limit.

[[:Category:Enemies with Barriers|Enemies with the Barrier ability]] are able to ignore any damage that is weaker than the limit of their Barrier as well as any status effects that would be inflicted by those attacks. Each enemy has a Barrier with different limit and it is not affected by strength magnification. If a single attack deals more damage to a Barrier than the Barrier's health value (including additional damage from abilities such as Massive Damage or Savage Blow), the Barrier will break. After breaking the Barrier, the enemy is vulnerable to all attacks and status effects; Cats with the Barrier Breaker ability have either a percentage chance or are guaranteed to break Barriers, without having to deal higher damage than the Barrier limit.

===Restrictions===
The majority of the stages in Cats of the Cosmos have Battle Restrictions. Every 3 stages has different restrictions, with a few exceptions. The restrictions are as listed:
*[[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]], [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]], [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]], [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]], [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] only
*Cats with ≥300¢ deployment cost only
*MAX number of 20 Cats
*Only deploy Cats in the first row
*Normal, [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]], Uber Rare, Legend Rare only
*Cats with ≤4,000¢ deployment cost only
*Special, Rare, Super Rare Cats only
*Cats with ≤1,200¢ deployment cost only
*MAX number of 15 Cats
*Special Cats only
*Cats with ≥1,200¢ deployment cost only
*MAX number of 10 Cats
*Special, Rare, Uber Rare, Legend Rare only

==Chapter 1: Beyond the Exosphere==
[[File:CotC1MenuButton.png|thumb]]
(にゃんこ軍団宇宙侵略！！ ''Nyanko Gundan Uchū Shinryaku!!'', '''Cat Army Invading the Cosmos!!''')
*Starred Aliens in this chapter have a strength magnification of 100%; other enemies' buffs are around [[Into the Future]] Chapter 2 levels.
*The final boss of this chapter is [[The Cat God]], with non-stop waves of Starred Alien peons.
*Players receive 100 [[Cat Food]] and unlock a 70% discount on all of [[The Cat God (Special Cat)|The Cat God]]'s miracles upon completion.
*Obtaining all Superior [[Treasure]]s in this chapter awards 3,000,000 XP.

==Chapter 2: The Passion of Catgod==
[[File:CotC2MenuButton.png|thumb]]
(激神！！神さまの本気！？ ''Gekishin!! Kami-sama no Honki!?'', '''Fierce God!! God is Serious!?''')
*Starred Aliens introduced in this chapter have a strength magnification of 100%.
*Old Starred Aliens not introduced in this chapter have a strength magnification of 131%-300%; [[:Category:Unstarred Alien Enemies|unstarred Aliens]] are even stronger than in Into the Future Chapter 3, and other enemies' buffs are around [[Body & Soul|sub-chapter 27]].
*The final boss of this chapter is [[Cat God]], with stronger waves of Starred Alien peons.
*Players receive 100 Cat Food and unlock [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]] upon completion.
*Obtaining all Superior Treasures in this chapter awards 4,000,000 XP.

==Chapter 3: Even Stars Burn Out==
[[File:CotC3MenuButton.png|thumb]]
(最後の戦い！神の顔も三度まで！？ ''Saigo no Tatakai! Kami no Kao mo Sando Made!?'', '''Final Battle! Even God Loses Patience After Three Times!?''')
*Starred Aliens introduced in this chapter have a strength magnification of 100%-900%.
*Old Starred Aliens not introduced in this chapter have a strength magnification of 150%-2500%; most other enemies' buffs can be compared with somewhere around [[Mouseyland|sub-chapter 36]].
*The final boss of this chapter is [[Final Boss Giga-God]], with even stronger—albeit limited—waves of Starred Aliens.
*Players receive 150 [[Cat Food]] along with a [[Platinum Capsules (Gacha Event)|Platinum Ticket]] upon completion.
*Also, clearing this chapter will give players access to [[Cat Capsule#Cat Capsules+|Cat Capsules+]], an upgraded version of [[Normal Cat Capsule]].
*After completing this chapter, there will be a [[Filibuster Invasion (Cats of the Cosmos)|bonus stage]] where [[Filibuster Obstructa]] will appear. Once the stage is completed, the player will unlock [[Filibuster Cat X (Special Cat)|Filibuster Cat X]].
*Obtaining all Superior Treasures in this chapter awards 5,000,000 XP.

==Zombie Outbreaks==
:''Main article: [[Zombie Outbreaks]]''
In Cats of the Cosmos' Zombie Outbreaks, the only restrictions to appear are Cat Deploy Limits of 5, 10, or 15, even in stages that normally have different restrictions. Chapter 2 deviates significantly from past Outbreaks by not only reintroducing several [[Legend Stages]] [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] like [[Zamelle]] and [[Formicidaean Ariant]], but also adding [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] and [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemies of other traits to many stages alongside the Zombies. See the Zombie Outbreaks article for more information.

